a writing standpoint  i just gobbled up all the zany subvision  wanda had to go through  and i would have been completely down if  that's what all the show was  another highlight to me is the complete  aura of mystery that everything is  shrouded in  for the first three episodes i actually  felt like one of those youtubers that  creates theories upon  every sort of evidence that they were  given the mystery aspect allowed for so  much input of brain power from the  viewer  to try and figure everything out then  when they actually reveal something  it's like a massive dopamine hit  watching that fourth episode and  witnessing the events from the  perspective of monica rambo  you were able to piece together that  puzzle before the characters did  and you feel like this you know i'm  something of a scientist myself  to me this felt very rewarding and once  the mystery drops off a bit  the creators shake things up with the  surprise return of quicksilver  and speaking of quicksilver this is one  of the things that kind of bothered me  i was one of those people who had their  mind blown when evan peters came back as  quicksilver  oh my god okay it's happening everybody  stay calm  only to be let down by the ending reveal  that he's just some random guy  this is twice now that marvel has  dangled the multiverse in our faces  and faked us out for the sake of a joke  boner  it was okay the first time and far from  home when mysterio was lying about there  being a multiverse  and that on its own was the big twist  but for one division  they are practically breaking the fourth  wall by casting evan peters as the  resurrected quicksilver  this does make the whole dynamic crazier  and funnier  but you're inevitably setting up people  for some amount of disappointments  especially since the fans know that the  multiverse is eventually coming  given that the doctor strength sequel  has the multiverse of madness in its  title  another aspect i have some mixed  feelings about was the reveal that  agatha was the villain  all along this felt jarring to me  because it came across that wanda was  the primary villain  and then the blame just got shifted to  someone else at the end  for the whole show it was very apparent  that wanda was in the wrong given that  she was enslaving a whole town of people  who are being mentally tortured and then  at the end  wanna just like oh yeah agatha showed me  i was being a dick so you guys can just  go now  i don't know why agatha would help her  come to the realization  when she was the one trying to sabotage  things to begin with  looking more at agatha she seemed pretty  cool and had some depth  but it felt jarring to drastically throw  the story in a different direction  towards the end of the show  i also rewatched the show while making  butt is full of memes  and i didn't see any clues pointing  towards agatha being the villain besides  her calling out monica rambo  if they left some more clues pointing  towards agatha being the villain then  maybe it wouldn't feel as jarring  it is hard to complain about it though  because i really enjoyed the second to  last episode  i think it was very clever to utilize  magic as a means to access someone's  memories  and thus build their character besides  using a generic flashback  we learned more about wanda's character  while also moving the story forward  which to me is overall great  storytelling then the final battle does  turn  towards the more special effect type of  battle but the way in which wanda and  vision outsmarted their enemies was very  clever also that shiba theseus scene has  already become a big meme  overall i feel like the last third of  the show fell apart a bit  it became messier with the drastic  change in direction  and there were some plot elements that  were not elaborated enough on  like monica rambo had a big scene where  she got her powers  and then it mostly gets dropped and  isn't explored properly  her character literally gets sidelined  by a quicksilver and she disappears for  a whole episode  that and when she breaks out and beats  quicksilver she doesn't even use her  powers to do so  when she does end up using her powers  she just awkwardly shows up at the end  to save wanda's fake  kids which in of itself is kind of  stupid because she knows they aren't  real and she is for some reason willing  to die for them  at that point in the story she didn't  know much about her powers  so it's weird that she made the decision  to risk her life for some pixels  besides the weaker last start of the  show i still think it was pretty great  i'd basically give it a 4 out of 5.  but yeah i hope you guys enjoyed the  video and let me know what you thought  about the show in the comments  you
 

